  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S Albanit & Co vs Union Territory Of J&K & Ors on 28 March, 2023 Author: Moksha Khajuria Kazmi Bench: Moksha Khajuria Kazmi Item No. 105 Supp. List High Court Of Jammu & Kashmir And Ladakh At Srinagar Wp ( C) No. 650/2023 Cm No. 1537/2023 M/S Albanit & Co. ...Petitioner(s) Through: Mr. Adil Asimi, Advocate. Vs Union Territory of J&K & Ors. ... Respondent(s) Through: Coram: Hon'Ble Ms. Justice Moksha Khajuria Kazmi, Judge Order",
    "facts": "It is urged that petitioners are the registered contractors dealing with the business of food services-restaurants for different hospitals, however, the tender issued by the respondent No. 4 is in violation of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. It is submitted that in view of the nature of food services and place, i.e., hospitals, the food service contractors who would be assigned the contract against any tender notice as per requirement must be an \"A\" class contractor with GST qualification, tax credentials and with high income source above crores which conditions has not been incorporated in the impugned tender notice by the respondent No. 4.",
